- op: discuss  # a500
  at: '2026-09-10T22:12:29Z'  # a500
  by: agent  # a500
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a500
  clock: 4  # a500
  nonce: a500  # a500
  message: "DONE — merged as PR #896, dev 2303bef742. Closed on the filed row.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. `_pool_repo_path` in `bakeoff-deep` and BOTH reflect scripts,\nmirroring `bakeoff-broad`'s existing helper: resolve through\n`pool_utils.resolve_repo_path`, fall back to the naive join so a genuinely\nmissing repo still errors where it errored before rather than passing None\ndownstream. The two agent-facing guidance strings that printed\n`<pool>/<repo_name>/` now say a repo may be nested one level.\n\nVERIFIED BEHAVIOURALLY, not by proxy. The filed repro was\n`bakeoff-deep cohort --repos django` succeeding while `bakeoff-deep run` died\nwith `FileNotFoundError: /home/jgstern_agent/ALL_REPOS/django`. After the fix the\nsame pool ran the full battery end to end: `deep-20260910-151249`, django\nresolved at `.../whole_bunch_of_repos/django`, 74 artifacts, 306s, rc=0. The\ndirected A/B that followed ran two more sessions over pretix + django on the same\npool with no path failure.\n\nTHE ENUMERATION WAS THE POINT. Fixing only the line that crashed would have left\n`bakeoff-deep-reflect:893` — INSIDE `bakeoff-deep cycle` — handing the reflect\nagent a source path that does not exist. That one does not crash; it reads\nnothing and reports quietly, so a cycle could select and analyse repos correctly\nand then verdict them on absence. WI-favav had already fixed this exact shape in\n`bakeoff-broad` and `bakeoff-deep` already cited WI-favav in its SELECTION path;\nonly the run path missed it. Two call sites fixed, three-plus missed, and the\nsilent one was the dangerous one.\n\nTESTS ARE SPLIT PER SCRIPT DELIBERATELY. A single family-wide file passed locally\nand would have passed CI on that PR, then never run again: the top-level test map\nselects root tests by name prefix and no name maps to four scripts. Its own guard\n`test_top_level_test_map.py::test_no_new_unreachable_top_level_tests` caught it.\nNaming each file after the script it covers was the honest fix rather than taking\nthe KNOWN_UNREACHABLE exemption, which exists for tests the mapper structurally\ncannot claim. Each copy carries the family-wide enumeration check, so touching\nany one of the four re-runs it across all of them — that is what a third partial\nfix would trip over.\n\nRESIDUAL, filed not folded: WI-zilar — `run`'s code-hash skip guard does not\ncheck that the previous run produced output, so the crash THIS item describes\npoisoned its session and later runs exited 0 citing an empty directory. The\ncorrect predicate already exists in the same function (the `--all` batch path\nchecks `os.listdir(out_dir)`).\n\nNOT TAGGED `awaits_bakeoff_validation`: this carries no quantitative\nbakeoff-improvement claim. It is a tooling fix whose evidence is a repro that\nstopped reproducing."  # a500
